git log --format='%h %s' | head -2; git diff HEAD~1 | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-900 | head -30"]], "output": "```console\naf45d4c Outline rev 12: P7 analytic noise part; acceptance table placement\n7417245 Outline rev 11: C9 per Brief rev 11 (kappa* net of null cells, C3, threshold floor); rev 9-11 record\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-# Outline — what the paper says and what carries it (revision 11: verdicts per claim; review #5 applied; Brief rev. 11: P6 κ* net of null cells, design-only control C3, threshold floor)\n+# Outline — what the paper says and what carries it (revision 12: verdicts per claim; review #5 applied; Brief rev. 12: P6 κ* net of null cells, control C3, threshold floor; P7 analytic noise part)\n-Source: `idea-repo` Brief revision 11 (the idea, the predictions P1–P5, the study design and cell budget), the objective (`story-repo`#1) and `prior_work.md`. This page says *what to test and where it shows*, never what a result must be. Every claim below has a \"refuted if\" line; a result that triggers it changes the claim, and I take it to `idea-repo` (see \"When results do not carry it\").\n+Source: `idea-repo` Brief revision 12 (the idea, the predictions P1–P5, the study design and cell budget), the objective (`story-repo`#1) and `prior_work.md`. This page says *what to test and where it shows*, never what a result must be. Every claim below has a \"refuted if\" line; a result that triggers it changes the claim, and I take it to `idea-repo` (see \"When results do not carry it\").\n-*What the paper says (rev. 7):* (a) verdict *not supported* by the rule (pooled point gain 0.034 < 0.05), worded as **no evidence of a useful data-computable bias score, not evidence of none**: the intervals [−0.28, 0.34] (leave-one-mechanism-out) and [−0.27, 0.22] (leave-one-family-out) contain both a useful and a useless score, on 6 mechanism groups and 7 families; this goes in the abstract and the C6 text. (b) **Absolute held-out R² of log|bias| beside every gain** (`bias_reference.csv`, 1215 cells): exact-theory prediction 0.987 (a ceiling that uses the true response; labelled so, not a competitor); every data-computable predictor is *below the constant*: S̄ −0.22, corner×curvature −0.10, S_adj (exploratory) −0.06, degree benchmarks −0.26 to −0.27; the Han–Ugander-style CV loss is also below the constant on the Tier A cells (−0.17 on log RMSE, `cv_benchmark.csv`\n+*What the paper says (rev. 7):* (a) verdict *not supported* by the rule (pooled point gain 0.034 < 0.05), worded as **no evidence of a useful data-computable bias score, not evidence of none**: the intervals [−0.28, 0.34] (leave-one-mechanism-out) and [−0.27, 0.22] (leave-one-family-out) contain both a useful and a useless score, on 6 mechanism groups and 7 families; this goes in the abstract and the C6 text. (b) **Absolute held-out R² of log|bias| beside every gain** (`bias_reference.csv`, 1215 cells): exact-theory prediction 0.987 (a ceiling that uses the true response; labelled so, not a competitor); every data-computable predictor is *below the constant*: S̄ −0.22, corner×curvature −0.10, S_adj (exploratory) −0.06, degree benchmarks −0.26 to −0.27; the Han–Ugander-style CV loss is also below the constant on the Tier A cells (−0.17 on log RMSE, `cv_benchmark.csv`\n-- **Main text, 6 figures + 2 tables**: Fig 1 (C4 regime map + sign-error panel + real-graph rows), Fig 3 (C2 bias vs SD with degree, with a second row of bias/SD vs p carrying C3), Fig 5 (C4 tiers), Fig 6 (C5 cluster designs), Fig 7 (C6 diagnostic, D vs tie cells, per-group gains), Fig 9 (C8 coverage). Tables 1 (mechanisms, calibration) and 2 (acceptance-rule criteria and verdict).\n+- **Main text, 6 figures + 2 tables**: Fig 1 (C4 regime map + sign-error panel + real-graph rows), Fig 3 (C2 bias vs SD with degree, with a second row of bias/SD vs p carrying C3), Fig 5 (C4 tiers), Fig 6 (C5 cluster designs), Fig 7 (C6 diagnostic, D vs tie cells, per-group gains), Fig 9 (C8 coverage). Tables 1 (mechanisms, calibration) and 2 (acceptance-rule criteria and verdict). *Placement change (`report`, to fit nine pages):* the acceptance \n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "89363e96-54d3-561a-a115-2672efad5e15", "at": 1795648452.9598434, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 78923, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "d6428e5797325647abb15753ac0a8b8e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "e755926d-bfc3-5b40-b5d7-8a41bb2f37e0", "at": 1795648452.967063, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 78924, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "d6428e5797325647abb15753ac0a8b8e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "ed51d069-dfbc-58d0-adf8-12e25ef95de3", "at": 1795648452.969609, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 78925, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "d6428e5797325647abb15753ac0a8b8e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "ebcdd95b-c004-5c75-b403-eb7997884e86", "at": 1795648453.0228918, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 78926, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "d6428e5797325647abb15753ac0a8b8e", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], 